  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [2518-LS, CMB-01, CMB-02, CMB-03, Flood Risk Assessment and Fire Safety Strategy].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - Any works permitted by this permission will have to confirm the piling activities will be taking place at low water, or if piling in water, confirm that adequate mitigation is in place to avoid potential negative sonic impacts especially concerning migratory fish. \r\nReason: To protect fish species [Atlantic Salmon, European Eel, Sea Lamprey, Twaite Shad, River Lamprey, Allis Shad and Smelt] for the duration of any works permitted by this permission. This is supported by national planning policy set out in paragraphs 187 and 192 of the National Planning Policy Framework and Hounslow's existing and upcoming Local Plan Policies GB6 (Residential Moorings) and GB7 (Biodiversity).\r\n"
